# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# Without this file a Windows checkout with the default core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# tracked text file to CRLF, so `git status` is noisy, diffs show whole files changed, and
# line-ending sensitive assertions read the wrong bytes. `text=auto` still lets git detect
# binaries (dylibs, .node, prebuilt exes, PNGs) and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exception: Windows tooling expects CRLF in these when they appear.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
